Author: Aron Xu <aron@debian.org>
Description: bump Linux-Maximum to declare Linux 7.1 support
 The Linux 7.1 dentry d_alias compatibility code (config/kernel-dentry-alias.m4
 and the HAVE_DENTRY_D_U_ALIASES wiring) is already present in the 2.4.3 release
 tarball, but META still declares Linux-Maximum: 7.0, so the autoconf
 kernel-version check refuses to build against Linux 7.1. Bump the field to 7.1
 to permit it.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/openzfs/zfs/commit/a35e8d892628d01e50af23aee5ba501be426baf6
Forwarded: not-needed
Index: zfs/META
===================================================================
--- zfs.orig/META
+++ zfs/META
@@ -6,5 +6,5 @@ Release:       1
 Release-Tags:  relext
 License:       CDDL
 Author:        OpenZFS
-Linux-Maximum: 7.0
+Linux-Maximum: 7.1
 Linux-Minimum: 4.18
